# Tab completion

When adding or changing commands, subcommands, flags, or arguments, implement tab completion to the fullest practical extent in the same change.

## Required coverage

- Subcommand names at every command level
- Dynamic values: session IDs, event names, online players, plugins, worlds
- Flag names (`--format`, `--shareable`, etc.) at any position after fixed arguments
- Flag values immediately after the flag token (formats, enums, booleans)
- Multiple flags on one command — completion must still work after earlier flags

## Rules

- Mirror the same valid values enforced by command parsing
- Prefer `CommandText.filterPrefix` for consistent partial matching
- Keep completers colocated with handlers (`*TabCompleter`, `tabComplete*` methods)
- When introducing a new flag or enum, add both parser validation and tab completion

## Checklist for new CLI surface

1. Usage string documents all flags and values
2. Parser rejects invalid values with a helpful error listing valid types
3. Tab completer suggests flags and value options at the correct argument index
